<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:h="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" version="1.0" name="VoiceSession" initial="idle"><metadata><h:section id="documentation"><h:h2>VoiceSession — actor contract</h:h2><h:p><h:strong>Actor invariant: </h:strong>VoiceSession owns Gemini Live socket and confirmed transcript, not MediaStream tracks. On mic lost send audio end, enter paused, preserve context; on new acquired track resume same session where available or reconnect with contextual replay.</h:p><h:p><h:strong>Specification: </h:strong>ACT-VOICE in <h:a href="../system.xml">system.xml</h:a>. These comments use XHTML namespace h: and are not executable SCXML actions.</h:p><h:h3>I/O contracts invoked by this actor</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-VOICE-CONNECT">review.voice.connect</h:a> — VoiceConnectRequest → VoiceConnectResult | Fault; external-write, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-006, FL-026; requirements: REQ-019, REQ-020, REQ-026, REQ-030</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-VOICE-STOP">review.voice.stop</h:a> — VoiceStopRequest → VoiceStopResult | Fault; local-write, safe-idempotent, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-006, FL-034; requirements: REQ-019, REQ-063</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-LIVE-TOKEN">review.gemini.mintLiveToken</h:a> — LiveTokenRequest → LiveTokenResult | Fault; external-write, safe-idempotent, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-006, FL-024, FL-027; requirements: REQ-029, REQ-030, REQ-035</h:li></h:ul></h:section></metadata><state id="idle">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-idle"><h:h3>State: idle</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>voice.start</h:code> → requesting</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="voice.start" target="requesting"/>
  </state>
  <state id="requesting">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-requesting"><h:h3>State: requesting</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>voice.connected</h:code> → listening<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-VOICE-CONNECT"> [typed result: IO-VOICE-CONNECT]</h:a></h:li><h:li><h:code>voice.failed</h:code> → failed<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-VOICE-CONNECT"> [typed result: IO-VOICE-CONNECT]</h:a></h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="voice.connected" target="listening"/>
    <transition event="voice.failed" target="failed"/>
  </state>
  <state id="listening">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-listening"><h:h3>State: listening</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>voice.transcript</h:code> → listening</h:li><h:li><h:code>voice.stop</h:code> → stopping</h:li><h:li><h:code>voice.paused</h:code> → paused</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="voice.transcript" target="listening"/>
    <transition event="voice.stop" target="stopping"/>
    <transition event="voice.paused" target="paused"/>
  </state>
  <state id="stopping">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-stopping"><h:h3>State: stopping</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>voice.stopped</h:code> → idle<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-VOICE-STOP"> [typed result: IO-VOICE-STOP]</h:a></h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="voice.stopped" target="idle"/>
  </state>
  <state id="failed"><metadata><h:section id="state-failed"><h:h3>State: failed</h:h3><h:p>No outgoing transitions in this version. This state is terminal until the host ends or restores the actor.</h:p></h:section></metadata></state>
  <state id="paused">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-paused"><h:h3>State: paused</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>voice.resumed</h:code> → listening</h:li><h:li><h:code>voice.stop</h:code> → stopping</h:li><h:li><h:code>voice.failed</h:code> → failed<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-VOICE-CONNECT"> [typed result: IO-VOICE-CONNECT]</h:a></h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="voice.resumed" target="listening"/>
    <transition event="voice.stop" target="stopping"/>
    <transition event="voice.failed" target="failed"/>
  </state>
</scxml>
